  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "Done — the only gap in this repo was item 12 (UC10 real export files); items 9, 10 and 11 are already implemented by the existing UC7/UC8/UC9 modules, and the eight tracker/contracts endpoints the counterpart named already exist here with the contract's spelling.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- **`app/services/export_files.py` (new)** — standard-library writers producing genuine files (CLAUDE.md forbids adding packages): `build_xlsx` emits a real `.xlsx` (zipped SpreadsheetML with inline strings), `build_pdf` emits a real PDF 1.4 with a paginated Helvetica text stream and a correct xref table.\n- **`app/services/tracker_export.py`** — `POST /api/v1/tracker/export` no longer returns a synthesized `fileUrl` with no bytes behind it. It now pulls the actual rows of the requested tab through that tab's own service (`tracker_ownership`, `tracker_cycle_time`, `tracker_bottleneck`, `tracker_turnaround`), so the file matches the current tab, period and filters, renders them to Excel or PDF, writes the bytes to `settings.export_storage_dir`, records them in `uploaded_files`, and returns `fileUrl`. The outcome tiers are unchanged: no contracts at all → `success=false`; zero rows for the period/filters → a file carrying a \"no records\" line; an unexpected failure → 2xx with `success=false` and \"Export failed. Please try again.\" (never an error status).\n- **`app/routers/tracker_export.py`** — added `GET /api/v1/tracker/exports/{fileId}` (same four roles) which streams the generated file with its content type and a `Content-Disposition` attachment name; this is what `fileUrl` points at.\n- **`app/repositories/files.py`** — a tenant-scoped `get_uploaded_file` lookup for that download.\n- **`app/config.py`** — `EXPORT_STORAGE_DIR` setting (default `var/exports`).\n- **`tests/test_tracker_export.py`** — the two happy-path tests now download the `fileUrl` and assert the bytes are a real xlsx (containing the Bottleneck columns and the seeded stage) and a real PDF; added a 404 test for an unknown export id, and an autouse fixture writing exports to a temp dir. Full suite: 503 passed.\n\nLeft for the other side: the search-term highlighting and the Excel/PDF format picker are presentation-only frontend changes.",
