    "notes": "Export now returns a real file: fileUrl is a relative path '/api/v1/tracker/exports/{fileId}' served by a NEW endpoint GET /api/v1/tracker/exports/{fileId} (same four roles) that returns raw xlsx/pdf bytes with Content-Disposition, not JSON — the frontend must prefix the API base URL and send auth. Failures are still 2xx with success=false plus failureMessage ('No contract data available to display.' or 'Export failed. Please try again.'); invalid tab/format/period/date-range are 400. Tab values are Ownership|CycleTime|Bottleneck|Turnaround and format Excel|PDF, matching the frontend. MISMATCH on GET /api/v1/contracts: this side does NOT accept searchText/startDateFrom/startDateTo/endDateFrom/endDateTo/valueMin/valueMax/folderTagIds/sortDirection and does not return the frontend's item fields (contractId/counterparty/value/owner/lastModified/folderTags/indexingInProgress); it accepts search/sortBy/sortOrder('asc'|'desc')/status/contractType/department/counterpartyId/ownerId/startDate/endDate and returns items with id/contractName/contractType/department/counterpartyName/contractOwnerName/status/startDate/endDate/contractValue/currency/riskScore plus page/pageSize/totalCount/noMatchMessage. Also note app/config.py now carries JWT login settings, so header-only auth may no longer be the whole story for callers."
